    summary:
      "A business-card-sized piece of papyrus in Coptic, announced in Rome in 2012, carrying a line in which a teacher speaks of his wife. Four years of scientific testing and scholarly argument ended when a magazine investigation traced its owner, and the historian who published it said the evidence now pressed towards forgery.",
