          "The second finding in that report is the one that should weigh most with a Christian reader. Several of the scientists whose early, cautious interest was quoted in support of the site later examined it properly and reversed their position — the geophysicist J. Baumgardner, who had worked with Wyatt at the site in the mid-1980s, came to hold firmly that it does not contain the ark — and their earlier remarks continued to be used after they had withdrawn them. The astronaut J. Irwin and the geologist J. Morris both inspected the site and were not persuaded. People were quoted as supporting a conclusion they had come to reject.",
